1️⃣ LeetCode #62 — Unique Paths

Medium

class Solution {
    public int uniquePaths(int m, int n) {
        int[] dp = new int[n];

        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
            dp[j] = 1;
        }

        for (int i = 1; i < m; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j < n; j++) {
                dp[j] = dp[j] + dp[j - 1];
            }
        }

        return dp[n - 1];
    }
}
🧠 Idea

Robot-ku 2 choices:

→ Right
↓ Down

Each cell-la:

ways = top + left

dp[j] old value = top
dp[j-1] = left

Time: O(m × n)
Space: O(n)

2️⃣ LeetCode #416 — Partition Equal Subset Sum

Medium ⭐

class Solution {
    public boolean canPartition(int[] nums) {
        int total = 0;

        for (int num : nums) {
            total += num;
        }

        if (total % 2 != 0) {
            return false;
        }

        int target = total / 2;

        boolean[] dp = new boolean[target + 1];
        dp[0] = true;

        for (int num : nums) {
            for (int sum = target; sum >= num; sum--) {
                dp[sum] = dp[sum] || dp[sum - num];
            }
        }

        return dp[target];
    }
}
🧠 Simple logic

Example:

[1,5,11,5]

Total:

22

Equal partition means:

11 + 11

So target = 11.

Question becomes:

"Can I select some numbers whose sum = 11?"

That's 0/1 Knapsack DP.

⚠️ Important:

for (int sum = target; sum >= num; sum--)

Reverse order → same number-a multiple times use panna prevent pannum.

Time: O(n × target)
Space: O(target)

3️⃣ LeetCode #1143 — Longest Common Subsequence

Medium ⭐

class Solution {
    public int longestCommonSubsequence(String text1, String text2) {
        int m = text1.length();
        int n = text2.length();

        int[] dp = new int[n + 1];

        for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {
            int diagonal = 0;

            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {
                int temp = dp[j];

                if (text1.charAt(i - 1) == text2.charAt(j - 1)) {
                    dp[j] = diagonal + 1;
                } else {
                    dp[j] = Math.max(dp[j], dp[j - 1]);
                }

                diagonal = temp;
            }
        }

        return dp[n];
    }
}
